questions.expected:
Identification is the username lookup, authentication is proof that the submitted secret matches the account, and authorization is the permission decision after identity is established.

```text
function $handle_request$(username, password, $requested_action$):
    user = find_user_by_username(username)        // identification
    if user is null:
        return deny("invalid credentials")

    if not $verify_password$(password, user.$password_record$):
        return deny("invalid credentials")        // authentication failed

    permissions = load_permissions_for(user)
    if $requested_action$ not in permissions:
        return deny("not authorized")             // deny by default

    return allow()
```
